1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,674
This tutorial covers the end of a tenancy
contract: renewing

2
00:00:03,674 --> 00:00:07,347
it, extending it, or ending it and
settling the deposit.

3
00:00:07,347 --> 00:00:10,653
As a Company Admin, open Leasing, then
Tenancy Contracts.

4
00:00:10,653 --> 00:00:13,592
Start with Ahmed Hassan's contract for
unit A-101,

5
00:00:13,592 --> 00:00:16,164
which ends on the thirty-first of
December.

6
00:00:16,164 --> 00:00:16,899
Select Renew.

7
00:00:16,899 --> 00:00:20,205
The next term, all of next year, is filled

8
00:00:20,205 --> 00:00:23,144
in, and the charge lines are copied
across.

9
00:00:23,144 --> 00:00:25,715
Choose By percent and enter 5, and

10
00:00:25,715 --> 00:00:28,287
the rent goes from 85,000 to 89,250.

11
00:00:28,287 --> 00:00:32,328
The deposit is carried forward, so it is
not collected again.

12
00:00:32,328 --> 00:00:33,062
Select Renew.

13
00:00:33,062 --> 00:00:35,634
A new draft opens for next year,

14
00:00:35,634 --> 00:00:37,838
linked to the contract it renews.

15
00:00:37,838 --> 00:00:41,144
It is signed and posted like any other
draft.

16
00:00:41,144 --> 00:00:45,185
An extension is for a shorter stay on the
same contract.

17
00:00:45,185 --> 00:00:47,757
Open Sara Mansour's contract for M-1501,
and

18
00:00:47,757 --> 00:00:49,961
under More actions, select Extend
Contract.

19
00:00:49,961 --> 00:00:53,634
Set the new end date to the thirty-first
of January.

20
00:00:53,634 --> 00:00:56,941
Add a Rent line of 9,500 for the extra

21
00:00:56,941 --> 00:00:59,880
month, and the cheque that pays for it.

22
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:00,982
Select Extend Contract.

23
00:01:00,982 --> 00:01:05,023
The end date moves, and the extension
posts its own entries.

24
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,594
Ending a contract starts with a notice.

25
00:01:07,594 --> 00:01:10,166
Open Rajesh Kumar's contract for A-103,
and

26
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:12,370
under More actions, select Give notice.

27
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:15,309
Rajesh gave notice on the thirty-first of
July,

28
00:01:15,309 --> 00:01:18,247
to move out on the thirty-first of August.

29
00:01:18,247 --> 00:01:21,921
Select Give notice, and the contract is
marked Notice Given.

30
00:01:21,921 --> 00:01:24,125
It keeps collecting until it ends.

31
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:26,697
Now select Terminate, and set the
termination

32
00:01:26,697 --> 00:01:28,901
date to the thirty-first of August.

33
00:01:28,901 --> 00:01:32,207
The figures show the rent earned to that
date,

34
00:01:32,207 --> 00:01:35,146
and the unearned rent that will be
reversed.

35
00:01:35,146 --> 00:01:38,452
Cheques dated up to the move-out are kept
for

36
00:01:38,452 --> 00:01:41,758
collection, and later ones go back to the
tenant.

37
00:01:41,758 --> 00:01:44,330
Add a note, select Terminate, and confirm.

38
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:47,269
The contract is terminated, and the
settlement opens.

39
00:01:47,269 --> 00:01:50,575
It shows the deposit held, and a
receivable balance

40
00:01:50,575 --> 00:01:53,881
below zero, because the landlord owes
Rajesh a little.

41
00:01:53,881 --> 00:01:56,453
Add a deduction for cleaning, of 1,500,

42
00:01:56,453 --> 00:01:58,657
and the refund drops to 11,612.33.

43
00:01:58,657 --> 00:02:01,596
Save draft keeps it for someone to review.

44
00:02:01,596 --> 00:02:04,535
Three kept cheques are still being
collected, so

45
00:02:04,535 --> 00:02:07,474
tick the confirmation, then select
Finalize, and confirm.

46
00:02:07,474 --> 00:02:10,412
The settlement is finalized with its own
journal,

47
00:02:10,412 --> 00:02:12,984
and the refund is ready to pay.
